Item_1_Comment:
To compare and combine effect sizes across different studies, we standardized the effect estimate of each air pollutant in these studies to a 10 μg/m3 change. First, we transformed parts per billion (ppb) to mass per volume unit (μg/m3) using the following formula: Conc1 = (Conc2 × M)/24.45 (1 atm, 25 °C), where M represents the molecular mass of a pollutant, and Conc1 or Conc2 represents the calculated or reported concentration of a pollutant, respectively (
Rouse et al., 2004
; 
Klepac et al., 2018
). Then, we calculated the standardized effect estimate for each air pollutant in each study using the following formula (
Rouse et al., 2004
; 
Yang et al., 2018
; 
Shah et al., 2013
): RR(standardized) = RRincrement (standardized)/increment (original) (original).

Item_2_Comment:
We used either a random-effects model or a fixed-effects model, depending on whether significant heterogeneity was present, and we generated forest plots to visualize the ORs and their 95%CIs (
Borenstein et al., 2010
).
